Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 23:19:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 117/138] media: apple: t7000 ISP: stages 8-9 (PRINT_ENABLE,
 START, CONFIG_GET, BUILDINFO) + graceful shutdown

Piece 4 of the IPC code, completing stages 7-9:
- stage 8: PRINT_ENABLE (opcode 4, 0xc bytes, enable = 1), then START
  (opcode 0, 8 bytes); both need status 0.
- stage 9: CONFIG_GET (opcode 3, 0x1c bytes) logged raw; BUILDINFO
  (opcode 6) where status 2 = not implemented is expected; the build
  string is taken from the fw header (+0x1060 / +0x1080).
- isp_fw_shutdown (kext ISP_deInit): STOP, gpio0 = 0xf7fbdff9, POWER_DOWN
  (0x10) without waiting, then <= 1 s for gpio0 == 0x8042006, 10 ms, and
  the existing CPU stop + power-off path. Skipped once IO timed out.
- SHAREDMALLOC replies zero words 1/2 like the kext (0x845ba18); a size
  below 0x1000 becomes 0x1000.
- isp-boot.c: include linux/mm.h for PAGE_ALIGN (W=1 build fix).

Builds as an external module (LLVM=1 W=1) without warnings, vermagic
7.3.0-rc1-gf689d352d4a8. Untested on hardware.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
